Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this statement unture. BSD's have good and versatile, specialized Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The BSD's have the flat out best Gift List in-Tribe, because they're designed as NPCs and their Gifts cover a lot of ground as the sole Wyrm Tribe instead of the 13 Gaian Tribe with their much less well rounded Gifts.<br /> <br /> Once we're talking about getting things out of Tribe, that's not important. It's not that their are only bad Gifts there you wouldn't want over the closest Gaian ones, but that, baring maybe a tiny number of exceptions, the in-game cost of learning a Gift from a Bane/corrupted spirit/etc. and the potential backlash against you for doing so (like being killed by the other Garou) is going to outweigh getting something that's mildly better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T13:42:25-07:00","id":1253994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1253967#post1253967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The BSD's have the flat out best Gift List in-Tribe, because they're designed as NPCs and their Gifts cover a lot of ground as the sole Wyrm Tribe instead of the 13 Gaian Tribe with their much less well rounded Gifts.<br /> <br /> Once we're talking about getting things out of Tribe, that's not important. It's not that their are only bad Gifts there you wouldn't want over the closest Gaian ones, but that, baring maybe a tiny number of exceptions, the in-game cost of learning a Gift from a Bane/corrupted spirit/etc. and the potential backlash against you for doing so (like being killed by the other Garou) is going to outweigh getting something that's mildly better.</div> </div> </div> </div>A better way then aura of poison to be able to approach and threaten a SAD or DNA Agent?<br /> <br /> Mental speech may not be quuite as imposing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T14:04:04-07:00","id":1253997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1253994#post1253994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A better way then aura of poison to be able to approach and threaten a SAD or DNA Agent?<br /> <br /> Mental speech may not be quuite as imposing?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you need to resort to Wyrmy gifts to face SAD or DNA agents, you are doing it wrong. To resort to Wyrmy gifts, the situation would have to be dire enough that it doesn't -matter- that you corrupt your soul. Garou can outwit human agents without selling their souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T14:29:44-07:00","id":1254002,"title":"","content":"Aura of Poison keeps things without Rage from attacking you without attacking first because you're scary. It doesn't actually help you approach or threaten anyone (they might just run from you since you're so scary).<br /> <br /> Persuasion doesn't cost a Gnosis, gives you a -2 difficulty break on all your social rolls for the scene, and your social rolls have greater impact than normal. So it's a perfect Gift for approaching a SAD or DNA agent (you can social roll them into listening to you without attacking) and then threaten them (the -2 difficulty and above normal impact is extremely potent). And it works on things with Rage.<br /> <br /> Brother's Scent is also a decent alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T14:32:51-07:00","id":1254003,"title":"","content":"1. I fully agree with Lian: The SAD simply doesn't have that depth of knowledge about the Garou. When investigating something, the closest they're likely to come is &quot;Yeah, I'd bet those claw marks could have come from a lycanthrope...&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. It's also irrelevant since (in canon at least) SAD no longer exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T16:50:15-07:00","id":1254026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1254002#post1254002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aura of Poison keeps things without Rage from attacking you without attacking first because you're scary. It doesn't actually help you approach or threaten anyone (they might just run from you since you're so scary).<br /> <br /> Persuasion doesn't cost a Gnosis, gives you a -2 difficulty break on all your social rolls for the scene, and your social rolls have greater impact than normal. So it's a perfect Gift for approaching a SAD or DNA agent (you can social roll them into listening to you without attacking) and then threaten them (the -2 difficulty and above normal impact is extremely potent). And it works on things with Rage.<br /> <br /> Brother's Scent is also a decent alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or really Blur of the milky eye, taking the Forgotten, Jam Tech...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T17:28:25-07:00","id":1254035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1254003#post1254003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I fully agree with Lian: The SAD simply doesn't have that depth of knowledge about the Garou. When investigating something, the closest they're likely to come is &quot;Yeah, I'd bet those claw marks could have come from a lycanthrope...&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. It's also irrelevant since (in canon at least) SAD no longer exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>officialy, yes they were all but disbanded. But theirs still a number of agents who do unofficial SAD stuff.<br /> <br /> Though I heard in V5 their involved in a &quot;Second inquisition&quot; I, personally, hate it as it steals my comic relief.<br /> <br /> <br /> I <i>like</i> to laugh at the feds<br /> <br /> And an idea on a better case to learn Wyrmish gifts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T18:05:11-07:00","id":1254040,"title":"","content":"If you want to laugh at the feds, be a Homid Glasswalker (esp. Ragabash, Philodox, or Galliard) and you'll have all the Gifts you need without having to worry about the complications of going Wyrmy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T09:11:08-07:00","id":1254234,"title":"","content":"some gifts youd suggest for putting SAD or DNA in their place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T13:11:43-07:00","id":1254318,"title":"","content":"Lian and I already gave examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T19:24:59-07:00","id":1254904,"title":"","content":"Werewolf hunters generally aren't scary for what they can do to werewolves, but rather what they can do to Cubs and Kin. the SAD agent is going to have to do serious work to hurt a starting Garou and it only gets worse from there... in a one on one encounter.<br /> <br /> The Danger of the SAD isn't that he's going to pull out the silver bullets. The danger is he's a federal agent. He can throw various powers of the Federal government at you and yours, and as a creature of rage who lives on the edge of society you don't want this. The Veil is important. The SAD is threat that could get your Caern on government lands sold to the highest bidder(Pentex obviously!) it can get your Kin arrested, hell even having an APB on you that you have to dodge and sneak around is an issue. This the problems the SAD brings and they aren't jokes.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if you're trying to incorporate the SI? Its even less of a joke because its the tool the Technocracy has decided to use to say &quot;We're done with your bullshit&quot; now that's crossover but the SI is pure crossover anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T09:02:18-07:00","id":1255012,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn a better example of something to learn Dancer gifts over?<br /> <br /> in Shadows of War (If anyone heres played it) Talion does something similar.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll leave it at that to avoid spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T14:21:53-07:00","id":1255092,"title":"","content":"Um... confused? What are you trying to say there? I mean, I haven't played Shadows of War (wasn't a big fans of Shadows of Mordor), so.. what are we talking about? And it's a game that's been out for a year in a very well known setting... I think we can risk a few spoilers (or at least but them in a spoiler box).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T23:29:34-07:00","id":1255662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmmn fair enough<br /> <br /> In shadows of war the protagonist in order to save middle earth becomes a Nazgul<br /> <br /> He chooses to wear one of the 9 rings of power to men, after destroying one of the Nazgul<br /> <br /> it was the only way to remain alive for him<br /> <br /> He valiantly goes on for decades fighting against Sauron, as the ring corrupted his mind. <br /> <br /> But in the end, when the ring is finished he becomes a willing slave.<br /> <br /> Only freed by the rings destruction. </div> </div> </div><br /> does that sound like a valid Comparison to what it is for a gaian garou to learn a dancer gift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T02:26:31-07:00","id":1255686,"title":"","content":"That's... pretty hard to put in WtA's framework. The closest version of that would be something a long the lines of a Gaian werewolf needing to do [something] necessary for the good of the cause, but despised enough that they get ostracized as a Ronin and continue to try to fight the good fight even as a Ronin the eventually fall prey to bad stuff.<br /> <br /> It's hard to imagine any Gift carrying that level of narrative weight though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T04:30:58-07:00","id":1255703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1255686#post1255686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... pretty hard to put in WtA's framework. The closest version of that would be something a long the lines of a Gaian werewolf needing to do [something] necessary for the good of the cause, but despised enough that they get ostracized as a Ronin and continue to try to fight the good fight even as a Ronin the eventually fall prey to bad stuff.<br /> <br /> It's hard to imagine any Gift carrying that level of narrative weight though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Closest I guess would be the way some Banetenders are seen....but yeah not really applicable and.....I can hear Tolkien doing about 800 rpm in his grave in regards to the video game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T05:08:42-07:00","id":1255712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1255703#post1255703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Closest I guess would be the way some Banetenders are seen....but yeah not really applicable and.....I can hear Tolkien doing about 800 rpm in his grave in regards to the video game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm pretty sure you can't 'tough it out' with all 9 rings XD<br /> <br /> The thing about BSD gifts, is that not even BSDs rely solely on them. They got auspice gifts and breed gifts just as any garou. Sure, they have ones solely for them, but they still use mother's touch as much as any Gaian.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T06:02:26-07:00","id":1255734,"title":"","content":"sadly, The video game is more faithful to tolkeins works then The movies have been... not that that is much of an accomplishment.<br /> <br /> Its possible for a dancer theurge to learn mothers touch but rare.<br /> <br /> a better idea for a case for a garou to learn a dancer gift?<br /> <br /> or is it best for 'Fringe camps' like &quot;Sword of heimdall&quot; <br /> <br /> as opposed to a real reason? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T14:19:55-07:00","id":1255883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1255734#post1255734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its possible for a dancer theurge to learn mothers touch but rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? It's one of their starting Gift options, it's 3 XP to pick up (even if they're not PCs with XP, it indicates the level of effort involved). BSDs get hurt and need patching up to throw back into the fight just like any other Garou. Not having medics is a pretty stupid idea if you're in the middle of a war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a better idea for a case for a garou to learn a dancer gift? </div> </div> </div>OK... why is this so important to have happen?<br /> <br /> Maybe if you come at this another way, we might be able to be more helpful. That games isn't written with the idea of the BSD Tribal Gift list as something the Gaian wolves are going to care about. It's not there to tempt them with awesome Gifts to try to corrupt them to the Wyrm's cause through bribery. Basically, BSD Gifts aren't designed for Gaians to learn, not as a mechanical issue, but as a narrative one.<br /> <br /> Garou get corrupted and fall to the Wyrm over more individualized methods that takes more work than waving cool powers in their face.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T16:30:07-07:00","id":1255945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1253805-can-black-spiral-dancer-gifts-be-learned-out-of-tribe?p=1255883#post1255883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? It's one of their starting Gift options, it's 3 XP to pick up (even if they're not PCs with XP, it indicates the level of effort involved). BSDs get hurt and need patching up to throw back into the fight just like any other Garou. Not having medics is a pretty stupid idea if you're in the middle of a war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OK... why is this so important to have happen?<br /> <br /> Maybe if you come at this another way, we might be able to be more helpful. That games isn't written with the idea of the BSD Tribal Gift list as something the Gaian wolves are going to care about. It's not there to tempt them with awesome Gifts to try to corrupt them to the Wyrm's cause through bribery. Basically, BSD Gifts aren't designed for Gaians to learn, not as a mechanical issue, but as a narrative one.<br /> <br /> Garou get corrupted and fall to the Wyrm over more individualized methods that takes more work than waving cool powers in their face.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I just thought it was an interesting question Patience of the wyrm still seems kind of cool if your a moderately vindictive sort, or want to do some sabotaging.<br /> <br /> on page 120 Book of the wyrm 20 it says clearly that dancer theruges rarely learn mothers touch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}